"""Source-authored bilingual manuscript. Review scope: depth-review-2026-10-20/REPORT.md."""
from model import p, ref, block, section

PART = dict(title=p('海關頒布的指引', 'Guidelines promulgated by the C&ED'),
intro=p('把法律要求落實成申請、處所、人員、評核及日常經營安排；貨幣兌換另須遵守第34章的顧客保障規則。', 'Translate the law into applications, premises, staffing, assessment and day-to-day operation. Money changing also engages Cap.34 consumer-protection rules.'), sections=[
section('premises', '營業處所、本地管理辦事處與紀錄儲存地方', 'Business premises, local management office and record storage', [
    block('三種地方的用途不同', 'Three places with different purposes', [
        ('「特定處所」是用來經營貨幣兌換或匯款的地方。指引第4.4段只是舉出例子，不是說必須同時自置或租用、掛招牌，並且已經完成客戶交易，才需要登記。這些例子包括：(1) 被佔用作經營金錢服務；(2) 被宣傳（包括招牌）為會見客戶的處所；(3) 經常由持牌人以業主或租戶身分控制。例如：一處地方已經掛出兌換招牌、用來會見顧客，即使某一天還沒做成一筆交易，仍可能屬於須登記的特定處所，不能要求三個例子同時齊備。對應：Licensing Guide paragraph 4.4。', '“Particular premises” are premises used to operate money changing or remittance. Paragraph 4.4 only gives examples. It does not require ownership or tenancy, advertising and a completed customer transaction all to exist before the premises must be registered. The examples are: (1) premises occupied for operating a money service; (2) premises advertised, including by a signboard, for meeting customers; and (3) premises regularly controlled by the licensee as landlord or tenant. For example: a place already advertised with an exchange signboard and used to meet customers may need to be registered even if no transaction has yet been completed that day. The three examples do not all have to be present at once.'),
        ('不是每到一個地方辦一點事，那個地方就變成你的特定處所。只是食肆或銀行的訪客或顧客，或純粹為了處理公司會計或法律文件而到會計師行或律師行，並不會使該處成為自己的特定處所。沒有固定處所的上門服務、在客戶辦公室會客，以及使用流動電子設備進行的交易，可以屬於無特定處所的經營模式；中文文本在這裡用了「只」來形容使用這類設備。店舖同時使用手機，並不會因此變成無處所經營；而無特定處所，仍然必須持牌。例如：一間已有店鋪的兌換店，職員有時用手機跟顧客確認匯率，不會只因為用了手機，就變成「無特定處所」模式。', 'Not every place you visit for a task becomes your particular premises. Being only a visitor or customer at a restaurant or bank, or visiting an accountant or solicitor solely to deal with company documents, does not make that place the MSO’s particular premises. Door-to-door service without fixed premises, meetings at a customer’s office, and transactions using mobile electronic devices, are examples of operating with no particular premises; the Chinese text says “only” using such devices. A shop does not become a no-premises operation merely because phones are also used, and a no-premises operation still requires a licence. For example: an exchange shop that already has a store, whose staff sometimes confirm a rate with a customer by phone, does not become a “no particular premises” operation merely because a phone was used.'),
        ('有些處所本身就不適合用來申請。不適合的例子包括：位於純住宅樓宇內的處所；另一名金錢服務經營者正在用來經營，或另一名申請人已經填報用來申牌或續牌的處所；入口是其他業務的範圍，未得其佔用人或業主准許或協助便不能進入；或招牌上的業務名稱與提交的商業登記不同。如果是混合商住的處所，還必須取得每名佔用人的書面同意，讓獲授權人進入視察。例如：單位裡還住着家人，即使其中一人已簽字同意海關進入，只要尚有一名佔用人未同意，便仍未符合這項要求。', 'Some premises are not suitable for an application. Unsuitable examples include premises in a wholly residential building; premises already used by another MSO, or already declared by another grant or renewal applicant; premises whose entrance is another business’s area and cannot be entered without that occupant’s or owner’s permission or assistance; and a signboard whose business name differs from the submitted business registration. Mixed commercial/residential premises need every occupant’s written consent for authorized persons to enter for inspection. For example: even if one family member living in the unit has signed a consent, the requirement is not met while any other occupant has not consented.'),
        ('沒有特定營業處所的經營者，必須維持一個本地管理辦事處（LMO）。這是香港的實體辦事處兼通訊地址，可以親身及以電話聯絡，並由獨資經營者、合夥人、董事、最終擁有人及／或合規主任駐守。不接受把經營者的住址或住宅處所，或其服務供應商（例如公司秘書、會計師行、律師行）的地址或處所，當作 LMO。租約條款或業主信件中，還須有業主准許作金錢服務用途的內容。已經有特定處所的金錢服務經營者，並不是全部都另外再需要一個 LMO。', 'An operator with no particular business premises must maintain a local management office (LMO). This is a physical Hong Kong office and correspondence address, reachable in person and by telephone, and staffed by the proprietor, a partner, a director, an ultimate owner and/or the CO. The operator’s own residential address or premises, or a service provider’s address or premises, such as a company secretarial firm, an accountant or a solicitor, is not accepted. Landlord permission for money-service use must appear in the tenancy agreement or in a landlord’s letter. Not every MSO that already has particular premises needs a separate LMO.'),
        ('不論有沒有特定營業處所，所有申請人都必須有一個香港實體的本地紀錄儲存地方（LPS），用來保存受持牌人控制的完整金錢服務交易帳目及紀錄。同樣不接受經營者的住址或住宅處所，或其服務供應商的地址或處所。如果申請未交所需的 LMO 或 LPS 資料，申請無效、不獲處理，這也可以成為拒絕發牌的理由。其後如果不能持續維持該地方，可引致暫時吊銷或撤銷。例如：把帳簿放在會計師行的地址，並不符合 LPS 的要求；所有申請人，包括已有店鋪的申請人，都必須有自己控制的香港實體儲存地方。', 'Whether or not the operator has particular business premises, every applicant must have a local place for storage of books and records. All applicants need a physical Hong Kong LPS holding the complete money-service transaction books and records under the licensee’s control. The operator’s residential address or premises, or a service provider’s address or premises, is not accepted. An application that is missing the required LMO or LPS information is invalid and will not be processed, and the omission can also be a ground for refusal. Failure to maintain the required place afterwards can lead to suspension or revocation. For example: keeping the books at an accountant’s office does not meet the LPS requirement. Every applicant, including one that already has a shop, needs a physical Hong Kong storage place under the licensee’s control.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第4.4–4.11段', '¶4.4–4.11', 'local place for storage of books and records'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('與其他業務同址及商業登記', 'Sharing with another business and business registration', [
        ('可以與其他業務共用處所，但金錢服務必須與其他業務清楚分隔和識別；與另一名金錢服務經營者共用處所來經營金錢服務，則不獲接納。另外必須持有由稅務局局長發出的有效商業登記證（BR）。沒有有效證明，可以使申請不獲處理；已獲發牌的，其牌照可被暫停或撤銷。', 'Premises may be shared with another business, but the money service must be clearly partitioned and distinguished from that other business. Sharing the premises with another MSO in order to operate a money service is not accepted. A valid Business Registration (BR) Certificate issued by the Commissioner of Inland Revenue must also be maintained. The absence of a valid certificate can prevent an application from being processed, or expose an existing licence to suspension or revocation.'),
        ('本地管理辦事處和本地紀錄儲存地方的業主，必須准許把該處用於金錢服務業務，並在租約或業主信件中列明。只提供一個物理地址，而沒有這項許可，並不足以符合指引。', 'For an LMO and an LPS, the landlord must permit the premises to be used for money-service business, and that permission must appear in the tenancy agreement or in a landlord’s letter. Simply supplying a physical address, without that permission, does not satisfy the Guide.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第4.7–4.8、4.11、4.15(c)段', '¶4.7–4.8, 4.11, 4.15(c)', 'must be clearly partitioned'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('application', '新牌申請：文件、面見及正式聲明', 'New applications: documents, interview and declarations', [
    block('完整申請的主要組成', 'Main components of a complete application', [
        ('新牌申請要用表格1，連同適用的補充表或附件，並按清單提交身分、公司與商業登記、業務計劃、打擊洗錢政策、處所及人員證明等。如果申請涉及特定營業處所，新牌及續牌都須至少提交兩張102×152毫米（4R）照片：一張內部、一張外部。每個另外用作 LMO 或 LPS 的處所，也須有同樣的照片。可以親身、郵遞或使用指定電子渠道提交。如果未在指明期限內交妥所需資料或文件，申請無效，不獲處理。', 'A new licence application is made on Form 1, together with the applicable supplements or annexes, and with the checklist evidence of identity, corporate and business registration, the business plan, the AML policy, and the premises and personnel. For particular business premises, a new or renewal application needs at least two 102×152 mm (4R) photographs: one interior and one exterior. Each separate LMO or LPS premises needs the same photographs. Submit by the prescribed in-person, postal or electronic routes. If the required information or documents are not provided within the specified period, the application is invalid and will not be processed.'),
        ('面見時須帶會面通知、繳費紀錄及相關文件正本，並在海關人員面前簽署牌照申請書，還須澄清及闡述已提交的業務計劃和打擊洗錢政策。獨資經營者須本人出席。合夥由每名合夥人書面授權的合夥人或員工出席；法團由董事會書面授權的董事或員工出席。獲授權的普通員工可以出席面見，但這並不會因此取得應考能力評核的資格。例如：公司派一名獲董事會授權的職員去面談，這是可以的；但不能因為這名職員有權出席面談，就當他也可以代替董事去應考能力評核。', 'At the interview, bring the notice, the payment record and the relevant originals. Sign the licence application in the presence of Customs officers, and clarify or elaborate the business plan and AML policy that have already been submitted. The proprietor must attend in person. A partnership sends a partner or employee authorized in writing by every partner. A corporation sends a director or employee authorized in writing by its board. An ordinary employee who is authorized to attend the interview is not, by that fact alone, eligible to sit the competence assessment. For example: the company may send a staff member authorized by the board to the interview. That does not mean the same staff member can take the assessment in place of a director.'),
        ('個人填表格3A，連同附錄I及II；法團則填表格3B。第5.8段的見證程序，特別針對表格3A的附錄I，不能籠統套用到所有表格。聲明人須在獲授權的海關人員、執業專業人士（例如律師、會計師、核數師）、公證人或太平紳士面前簽署。見證人核對身分證明文件正本與所列個人資料，證明資料真確，並證明簽署是在其面前作出。對應：Licensing Guide paragraph 5.8。', 'Individuals complete Form 3A, with Appendices I and II. Corporations use Form 3B. The witnessing procedure in paragraph 5.8 applies specifically to Appendix I of Form 3A, and should not be applied indiscriminately to every form. The declarant signs before an authorized Customs officer, a practising professional such as a solicitor, accountant or auditor, a notary public, or a Justice of the Peace. The witness checks the particulars against the original identity documents, certifies that they are accurate, and certifies that the signature was made in the witness’s presence.'),
        ('處理時間沒有固定保證。所需時間要視乎何時收齊文件、處所實地視察、向其他機關索取適當人選判定紀錄，以及完成能力評核。海關會核對本部門、其他政府部門及執法機構所持有的資料。', 'There is no guaranteed fixed processing period. The time needed depends on collecting the documents, inspecting the premises, obtaining fitness-test records from other authorities, and completing the Assessment. Customs checks information held by itself, by other government departments and by law-enforcement agencies.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第4.15、5.1–5.9、6.3段及附件', '¶4.15, 5.1–5.9, 6.3; annexes', 'Form 3A'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('證明文件按身分及用途準備', 'Evidence by legal form and purpose', [
        ('證明文件要按法律形式準備，而且這些公司文件並不是金錢服務經營者的半年交易申報表。獨資或合夥提供有效商業登記及商業登記冊資料摘錄。本地公司另備成立證明、最新周年申報表 NAR1 及其後所有登記文件；新公司用 NNC1（股份有限公司）或 NNC1G（股份有限公司以外的公司）。非香港公司備非香港公司註冊證明、最新周年申報表 NN3 及其後存檔文件；新成立公司用 NN1（在香港註冊的非香港公司詳情）。另須按清單備章程及集團架構或持股比例。', 'Supporting documents depend on the legal form, and these corporate documents are not an MSO’s half-yearly transaction return. Proprietors and partnerships provide a valid business registration certificate and business-register extracts. Local companies also provide the certificate of incorporation, the latest annual return NAR1 and all subsequent filings. New companies use NNC1 (limited by shares) or NNC1G (not limited by shares). Non-Hong Kong companies provide their non-Hong Kong company registration certificate, the latest annual return NN3 and subsequent filings. Newly established companies use NN1 (particulars of a non-Hong Kong company registered in Hong Kong). The constitution and the group or ownership structure must also be added as listed.'),
        ('每個適用處所、LMO 及 LPS，都要提供已加蓋印花的租約或業權證明、平面圖、內外兩張 4R 照片，以及業主准許作指定用途的信件。LMO 另備有效商業登記；商住處所另備全體佔用人的同意。', 'For each applicable premises, LMO and LPS, provide the stamped tenancy or ownership document, a floor plan, two interior and exterior 4R photographs, and the owner’s permission for the relevant use. An LMO also needs a valid business registration. Mixed premises also need every occupant’s consent.'),
        ('獨資經營者，以及每名個人合夥人、董事及最終擁有人，須備表格3A連同附錄I及II。香港居民備香港身分證複本，非香港居民備旅遊證件個人資料頁複本。法人合夥人或董事備表格3B。本地或非香港公司另備有效商業登記、相應註冊證明及組織章程大綱或細則。未在港註冊的法團，則備按第32B章《公司（表格）規例》第3條核證的成立證明或等同文件。', 'The sole proprietor, and every individual partner, director and ultimate owner, provide Form 3A with Appendices I and II. Hong Kong residents provide a copy of the Hong Kong identity card; non-residents provide a copy of the biodata page of a travel document. Corporate partners or directors provide Form 3B. Local or non-Hong Kong companies also add a valid business registration certificate, the corresponding incorporation or registration certificate, and the memorandum and articles. A corporation that is not registered in Hong Kong provides incorporation or equivalent evidence certified under regulation 3 of the Companies (Forms) Regulations, Cap. 32B.'),
        ('業務計劃及打擊洗錢政策，須由適用的獨資經營者，以及每名個人合夥人、董事及最終擁有人確認。清單另外還包括本地或境外第三方合約、合規主任或洗錢報告主任的身分證、有效僱傭合約，以及申請日期前3個月內發出的地址證明、銀行戶權證明，以及銀行確認該戶口作金錢服務用途。第16.1段要求文件蓋上申請人的公司印章。清單並非盡錄，海關可以再索取資料。', 'The business plan and the AML policy must be endorsed by the applicable proprietor, and by every individual partner, director and ultimate owner. The checklist also covers local or foreign third-party contracts; the CO’s or MLRO’s identity card; valid employment contracts; address proof issued within three months before the application; evidence of bank-account ownership; and the bank’s acknowledgement that the account will be used for money service. Paragraph 16.1 requires the documents to be stamped with the applicant’s company chop. Customs may request more. The checklist is not exhaustive.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第16.1–16.3段，項目1–6', '¶16.1–16.3, items 1–6', 'Checklist for submission of supporting documents'),
    ], kind='reference'),
    block('理解：業務計劃與打擊洗錢政策各要說明甚麼', 'Understand: what the business plan and AML policy explain', [
        ('業務計劃須綜合概述整個業務，包括詳細運作模式、組織架構、支付系統、目標客戶、職員編制及財政等。如果不用銀行帳戶來經營，必須具體交代在這種安排下如何運作。「不經銀行」並不是可以省略支付路徑的理由。', 'The business plan should give a comprehensive overview of the business, including the detailed operating mode, organisational structure, payment system, target customers, staffing and finances. If the business will operate without a bank account, explain how it will operate under that arrangement. Not using a bank is not a reason for omitting the payment route.'),
        ('打擊洗錢政策則要說明，機構本身相關業務的政策、程序及管控，如何減低它所面對的洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集風險，以及如何符合規定。例如須闡述匯款的支付或結算系統，以及制裁篩查和高風險客戶篩查機制。只寫一句「本公司遵守法例」，並不足以說明上述內容。', 'The AML policy should explain the business’s own policies, procedures and controls for mitigating its money-laundering and terrorist-financing risks and for meeting the requirements. Examples include explaining the remittance payment or settlement systems, and the mechanisms for sanctions screening and high-risk-customer screening. A statement that the company complies with the law does not, by itself, explain these elements.'),
        ('首次申牌時，每一個額外營業處所都列入同一份申請，逐個繳付附加費，不必為每一個處所另外再交一份新牌申請。收費數字見第3部分「附表3：金錢服務牌照費用」。如果是已經持牌之後才新增處所，則須按下文的表格5事先申請。', 'At the initial application, include each additional business premises in the same application and pay the fee for each one. A separate new-licence application is not needed for every premises. The amounts are in Part 3, under Schedule 3 MSO licensing fees. Adding premises only after a licence has already been granted instead requires a prior application using Form 5, described below.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第2.6、5.2、8.4段', '¶2.6, 5.2, 8.4', 'detailed operation mode'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('發牌審查：拒絕理由須連同適用條件讀', 'Grant assessment: read refusal grounds with their conditions', [
        ('申請為甚麼會被拒絕，要連同發牌的法定前提一起讀，不能因為指引寫「可拒絕」，便當成這些條件可以任意豁免。第5.10段列舉的申請缺失包括：適當人選判定不合格、處所不合適、商住處所欠每名佔用人同意、欠 LPS 資料，以及無特定處所經營而欠 LMO 資料。處所適合，以及所需的佔用人同意，是法例上的發牌前提。', 'The grounds on which an application may be refused must be read together with the statutory conditions for grant. The Guide’s “may refuse” wording does not make those conditions freely waivable. Paragraph 5.10 lists fitness-test failure, unsuitable premises, missing consent from every occupant of mixed premises, missing LPS information and, for no-particular-premises operation, missing LMO information. Suitable premises, and the required occupant consent, are statutory conditions for grant.'),
        ('同一段還有其他拒絕理由的例子，而且交齊文件並不保證一定獲牌。其餘例子是：業務計劃或打擊洗錢政策不符合相關指引、未委任合資格的合規主任或洗錢報告主任、申請不完整或無效、沒有高級管理層應考或取得合格，以及本身屬 section 25 的豁免者。已獲法定豁免者的申請，依第3.1段不獲接納。這只是列舉拒絕理由。', 'The same paragraph has further examples of refusal grounds, and submitting a complete set of documents is not a guarantee that a licence will be granted. Further examples are a business plan/AML policy not meeting the relevant guidelines, no competent CO or MLRO, an incomplete or invalid application, no senior manager attending or passing, and section 25 exemption. Applications by exempt persons are not accepted under paragraph 3.1. This is a list of refusal grounds, not a promise that documents will secure a licence.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第3.1、5.10段', '¶3.1, 5.10', 'none of the senior management of an applicant'),
        ref('04', '第30(3)條', 's.30(3)', 'the premises are suitable'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('fitness', '適當人選：持續而非一次性的要求', 'Fitness and propriety: an ongoing requirement', [
    block('法定因素與補充評核', 'Statutory and supplementary factors', [
        ('適當人選是一項持續要求，不是獲牌時過一次關便永遠沒事。須考慮指定的香港或境外罪行，以及下一段所列的其他法定事項。被定罪，或出現某一項負面因素，並不必然自動失格；關長會按全部相關情況作整體判斷。獲牌之後，仍須持續符合。例如：多年前一次定罪，不會自動等於今天一定不合格；但獲牌之後如果再出現新的規管違規或誠信問題，適當人選仍然會被重新評估。', 'Fitness and propriety is an ongoing requirement. Passing the test at the time of grant does not make it a once-and-for-all exercise. Consider statutory Hong Kong/overseas offences and the other mandatory factors set out next. A conviction, or a single adverse factor, does not automatically determine failure. The CCE assesses all of the circumstances. Fitness and propriety continues after licensing. For example: a conviction from many years ago does not automatically mean the person must fail today. But if new regulatory breaches or honesty issues arise after licensing, fitness can still be reassessed.'),
        ('除了法例列明的事項，兩份補充指引還加了其他評核角度。第10份指引補充：不遵守 AMLO、牌照條件或其他規管義務、誠信或刑事紀錄，以及財政狀況。第11份再涵蓋對顧客是否公平、是否準備並能持續提供服務、合規主任等人員的能力或知識、評核表現、資料是否真確，以及是否配合海關。', 'Besides the matters listed in the Ordinance, two further guides add other assessment angles. Document 10 adds AMLO/licence/regulatory compliance, honesty or criminal history, and financial standing. Document 11 further considers fair treatment of customers, readiness and ability to provide services, the competence or knowledge of the CO and other personnel, assessment performance, whether information is truthful, and cooperation with Customs.'),
        ('其他還可能考慮的因素包括：組織、人手、財政及系統資源、有效的內控或審核、利益衝突、其他罪行或待決控罪、專業或監管譴責、其他牌照限制、董事失格、未清償的判決債項，以及其他業務帶來的洗錢或財務風險。停業很久，或空有牌照而沒有提供服務的準備，也可以影響判斷。', 'Other factors that may be considered include organisation, staffing, financial and systems resources, effective internal controls or audit, conflicts of interest, other offences or pending charges, professional or regulatory censure, restrictions on other licences, director disqualification, unsatisfied judgment debts, and money-laundering or financial risks from other businesses. Long inactivity, or holding a licence without being ready to provide the service, can also matter.'),
    ], [
        ref('10', '第4–6段', '¶4–6', 'bankrupt'),
        ref('11', '第5–7段', '¶5–7', 'conflict of interest'),
        ref('05', '第7.1–7.2段', '¶7.1–7.2', 'fit and proper'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('適當人選：法定必考慮的事項', 'Fitness and propriety: the statutory mandatory factors', [
        ('香港定罪這一項，範圍不只是「有沒有洗過錢」，也包括指定的不披露、通風報訊及不配合監管等行為。它包括 AMLO section 30(4)(a) 指明的罪行，涵蓋盡職審查、視察或調查、妨礙或虛假資料，以及審裁處等事宜；UNATMO section 14 的罪行；DTROP section 25(1)、25A(5) 或 (7) 及附表1的罪行；以及 OSCO section 25(1)、25A(5) 或 (7) 及附表1或2的罪行。', 'The Hong Kong conviction limb is wider than “whether the person has laundered money”. It also covers specified disclosure, tipping-off and supervisory-compliance offences. Hong Kong convictions include the AMLO offences specified in section 30(4)(a), covering CDD, inspection or investigation, obstruction or false information, and tribunal matters; UNATMO section 14; DTROP sections 25(1), 25A(5) or (7) and Schedule 1 offences; and OSCO sections 25(1), 25A(5) or (7) and Schedule 1 or 2 offences.'),
        ('境外定罪，以及破產或清盤等事項，同樣必須考慮，而且關長還須考慮其認為有關的任何其他事宜，不是只有一張定罪清單。境外定罪包括：若在香港作出便會構成上述罪行的行為、洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集，以及定罪必須裁定存在欺詐、貪污或不誠實的罪行。另須考慮持續不遵從 AMLO 或 section 51 規例；個人的未解除破產或破產程序；以及公司的清盤、清盤令或接管人。', 'Foreign convictions, and matters such as bankruptcy or winding-up, must also be considered. The CCE must also have regard to any other matter it considers relevant; this is not only a conviction checklist. Foreign convictions include conduct that would constitute those offences in Hong Kong, money-laundering or terrorist-financing offences, and offences that require a finding of fraud, corruption or dishonesty. Also consider persistent non-compliance with the AMLO or with regulations under section 51; an individual’s undischarged bankruptcy or bankruptcy proceedings; and corporate liquidation, a winding-up order or receivership.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '第30(4)條', 's.30(4)', 'acted fraudulently, corruptly or dishonestly'),
        ref('05', '第4.3段', '¶4.3', 'undischarged bankrupt'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('投訴、調查及財政誠信的例子', 'Complaints, investigations and financial-integrity examples', [
        ('整體評估還可以考慮合理而且出於真誠的客戶投訴；在任何司法管轄區的刑事或紀律程序、已通知的可能程序，或可能導致該等程序的調查；以及與債權人的妥協或安排。投訴或調查本身，並不會自動證明有罪或不適當，仍須按完整個案來評估。', 'A holistic fitness assessment may also consider reasonable customer complaints made in good faith; criminal or disciplinary proceedings in any jurisdiction, notified potential proceedings, or investigations that may lead to such proceedings; and compromises or arrangements with creditors. A complaint or an investigation does not, by itself, automatically establish guilt or unfitness. The whole case still has to be assessed.'),
    ], [
        ref('11', '第6(d)、(e)、(q)段', '¶6(d), (e), (q)', 'has been notified of any potential proceedings'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('assessment', '能力評核：誰參加、何時參加及合格標準', 'Competence assessment: participants, timing and pass criteria', [
    block('提名及重新評核', 'Nomination and reassessment', [
        ('能力評核不是人人都要考，但必須有合資格的高級管理層通過。最少一名負責監督打擊洗錢政策或程序、並對合規承擔管理責任的高級管理人員，必須通過評核。獨資經營者須本人參加。合夥或公司最多提名3名屬自然人的合夥人或董事，並且須在同一場次參加。', 'Not every staff member has to sit the competence assessment, but a qualifying member of senior management must pass it. At least one senior manager overseeing AML policies/procedures and accountable for compliance must pass. The sole proprietor attends personally. A partnership or corporation may nominate up to three natural-person partners or directors, and they must all sit in the same session.'),
        ('新牌和續牌的應考時限不同，也不要跟法定「屆滿前45日」的續牌申請期限混在一起。新牌申請須在與海關面見當日起計30日內參加。需要評核的續牌申請人，則在收到邀請後30日內參加。續牌提名的時限，見下文。', 'The time for sitting the assessment is not the same for a new application and a renewal, and it must not be mixed up with the statutory deadline for filing a renewal application at least 45 days before expiry. New applicants must attend within 30 days upon attending the Customs interview; renewal applicants requiring assessment attend within 30 days after receipt of invitation. The renewal nomination clock is set out below.'),
        ('合夥或公司的通過人士如果全部離任，通過狀態便會失效；須在向海關具報合夥人或董事變更當日起計30日內安排評核。如果須於180日內續牌，則按第4.6段的續牌評核安排辦理。第8.2段不適用於獨資經營的持牌人。', 'If all of a partnership’s or a company’s passing nominees leave, the passing status lapses. Assessment must then be arranged within 30 days upon notifying Customs of the change of partners or directors. If renewal falls within 180 days, follow the renewal-assessment arrangements in paragraph 4.6. Paragraph 8.2 does not apply to a sole-proprietor licensee.'),
        ('第一次未通過之後，還有另一次機會，但時間是「成績通知發出當日起計30日後」，不是「30日內」，也不表示可以無限次重考或自動延長牌照。續牌的重考，還必須在牌照屆滿前完成。英文原文是 after 30 days upon notification of result；中文原文以成績通知發出作為起算事件。例如：星期一收到不合格通知，不能在當週立即重考，而須等到通知發出當日起計30日之後；如果是續牌，還必須趕在舊牌屆滿前考完。', 'A first failure is not the end of the matter, but the retake is allowed only after a waiting period, not immediately, and not without limit. Following failure, a further opportunity is given to retake after 30 days upon notification of result; the Chinese original specifies the issue of the result notification as the starting event. A renewal retake must also be completed before the licence expires. “After 30 days” is not “within 30 days”, and it does not mean unlimited retakes or an automatic licence extension. For example: if a fail result is issued on a Monday, the candidate cannot retake later that week, and must wait until after 30 days beginning on the date the notification is issued. For a renewal, the retake must still be finished before the old licence expires.'),
        ('考試有35題，分為7個部分，每部分5題，作答時間75分鐘，每題只有一個答案。要合格，整體最少須答對25題，而且每個部分不可錯多於2題。即使總分已夠，只要其中一個部分只對了2題，仍然不合格。通過評核本身，也不保證一定獲發牌或續牌。例如：整體對了28題，但其中一個部分5題只對了2題（錯了3題），仍然不合格。', 'The paper has 35 questions, five in each of seven Parts, lasts 1 hour and 15 minutes, and allows only one answer to each question. To pass, you need at least 25 correct overall, and no more than two wrong in any Part. A sufficient total with only two correct in one Part still fails. Passing the assessment does not, by itself, guarantee a licence or a renewal. For example: a candidate who scores 28 overall, but who has only two correct (and therefore three wrong) in one Part, still fails.'),
        ('官方樣題會用到由多個陳述組成的組合選項，但每題仍然只選一個答案。複習時須理解每項陳述的條件和例外，而不是去背選項字母。對應：document 02（只用於理解題型）。', 'The official specimen questions use combination options that contain several statements, but each question still has only one answer. When revising, learn the conditions and exceptions of each rule, rather than memorising option letters. Document 02 is for understanding the format only.'),
        ('主要出題依據，是《打擊洗錢條例》、《打擊洗錢指引》、《金錢服務經營者牌照申請指引》，以及海關其他相關指引或通函。這並不是一份只包含文件01至24及26的封閉書目；01至24及26，是本套筆記選定的原文範圍。樣題只展示題型，不能用來縮小知識範圍，或推算考點出現的頻率。對應：document 01 paragraph 6.1。', 'The main sources for the questions are the AMLO, the AML Guideline, the Licensing Guide, and other relevant Customs guidelines or circulars. That is not a closed list consisting only of documents 01 to 24 and 26. Those documents are the selected originals for this set of notes. The specimen questions illustrate the format. They do not narrow the knowledge scope, or establish how often a topic will appear. This is document 01 paragraph 6.1.'),
    ], [
        ref('01', '第3–8段', '¶3–8', '1 hour and 15 minutes'),
        ref('02', '例1–7（只用於理解題型）', 'Examples 1–7 (format only)', 'Answer: d'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('應考及結果', 'Attendance and results', [
        ('應考當日須攜有照片的身分證明、列印出來的邀請，以及適用的授權信；遲到不准入場。文具由場地提供，並須遵守禁止電子設備及通訊的規則。答案填在指定答題紙上；同一題如果填了多於一個答案，該題不給分。', 'On the day, bring photo identification, a printed invitation, and any applicable authority letter. Late entry is refused. Stationery is supplied, and the restrictions on electronic devices and communication apply. Answers must be entered on the designated answer sheet. If more than one answer is marked for the same question, that question receives no credit.'),
        ('成績會在考試結束後14日內，只以電郵通知通過或不通過，須保留該通知作為日後證明。如果要求覆檢，須在成績通知發出當日起計7日內以書面提出；海關則在接獲要求當日起計14日內書面回覆。覆檢針對的是答題紙上的技術錯誤，例如分數輸入或數據不一致，結果為最終決定。不會提供實際分數、試題及正確答案。', 'Results are issued as a pass or fail, by email only, within 14 days after the Assessment. Keep the notification as evidence. A request for rechecking must be made in writing within seven days after the date the result notification is issued. Customs then replies in writing within 14 days after receiving the request. Rechecking addresses technical errors on the answer sheet, such as incorrect mark entries or inconsistent data, and the result is final. Exact scores, the questions and the correct answers are not disclosed.'),
        ('惡劣天氣會不會改期，要看當天早上8時或以後的警告信號。如果在這個時段懸掛八號或以上風球，或發出黑色暴雨警告，該場次會改期；三號風球，或黃色或紅色暴雨警告，通常照常舉行。實際場次仍須依照邀請及海關通知。', 'Whether bad weather leads to a postponement depends on the warning in force at or after 8 a.m. that morning. Under the guide’s weather arrangements, a No. 8 or higher signal, or black rain, at or after 8 a.m. suspends the session. A No. 3 signal, or amber or red rain, normally means the session proceeds. Follow the actual invitation and any Customs notices.'),
    ], [
        ref('01', '第8–13段', '¶8–13', '14 days'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('提名及例外的限制', 'Nomination and discretionary exceptions', [
        ('每次適用的新申請、沒有通過人士的續牌，或唯一通過人士離任的情況，按指引只作一次提名。如果沒有通過人士而仍要繼續營業，不是經營者可以自行宣布豁免；關長的有限酌情及其條件，見下文。', 'Nomination is not an unlimited right. The guide permits one nomination for each applicable new application, renewal without a passer, or loss of the only passer. Continuing to operate with no passer is not a self-declared exemption; the CCE’s limited discretion, and the conditions that accompany it, are set out below.'),
    ], [
        ref('01', '第4.4、8.3段', '¶4.4, 8.3', 'only for once'),
        ref('05', '第6.2段', '¶6.2', 'receipt'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('續牌提名七日與應考三十日', 'Renewal nomination in seven days versus attendance in thirty', [
        ('續牌如果需要評核，有兩個不能互換的時限：收到提名邀請函後7日內，提名合資格人士；獲提名者則在收到邀請函後30日內應考。七日是提名，三十日是應考。如果未在七日內提名，續牌申請便會無效，舊牌照到期時失效。例如：邀請函星期一收到，最遲須在起計7日內完成提名。提名做完之後，獲提名者還有另一段30日的應考期。把兩個期限記反，或過了7日才提名，都可以讓續牌申請無效。', 'If assessment is needed for a renewal, there are two clocks that must not be swapped. Where assessment is required for renewal, nominate eligible person(s) within seven days after receiving the invitation; nominees attend within thirty days after receiving it. Seven days is for nomination; thirty days is for attendance. Failure to nominate within the seven days invalidates the renewal, so the old licence lapses at expiry. For example: if the invitation arrives on a Monday, nomination must be completed within seven days beginning then. After nomination, the nominee still has a separate 30-day period in which to sit the paper. Mixing the two deadlines up, or nominating after the seven days have passed, can invalidate the renewal application.'),
        ('誰算「合資格人士」，不能用「獲授權去面談的職員」來代替。合資格人士須是監督金錢服務的高級管理層，直接參與公司政策或管治決策，並對合規職能及制度負責。須應考的提名人，必須是合資格的獨資經營者、合夥人或自然人董事。', 'Who counts as an “eligible person” cannot be replaced by “the staff member authorized to attend the interview”. An eligible person is senior management who oversees the money service, is directly involved in policy or governance decisions, and is accountable for compliance functions and systems. The assessment nominee must be an eligible sole proprietor, partner or natural-person director. An employee authorized only to attend a licensing interview does not, by that fact, take that person’s place.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第5.5、6.2、6.4(c)段', '¶5.5, 6.2, 6.4(c)', 'within seven days upon receipt of the invitation letter'),
        ref('01', '第4.1–4.3段', '¶4.1–4.3', 'has a direct involvement'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('以公司為單位的資格及有限酌情權', 'Company-based qualification and limited discretion', [
        ('提名只在第4.4段列明的情況作出一次：新牌申請；屆滿前90日內，而且沒有已通過評核的合資格人士；或已經具報唯一通過人士卸任。這項資格是以公司為單位的，不是每名通過人士都可以自由拿到任何其他公司去用的通行證。例如：甲公司的董事在甲公司通過了評核，並不能把這個結果直接帶到乙公司，當成乙公司已經有人通過。', 'Nomination is not available whenever someone happens to want it. Nomination is made once in the paragraph 4.4 circumstances: a new application; within 90 days before expiry where no eligible person has passed; or notification that the only passing eligible person has left. The qualification is company-based. It is not a freely transferable pass that any successful candidate can take to any other company. For example: a director who has passed in Company A cannot simply carry that result to Company B and treat Company B as already having a passer.'),
        ('如果沒有合資格人士通過，關長可以按個別情況酌情，准許持牌人繼續經營。批給豁免時，會施加其認為適當及必要的發牌條件，以確保有有效的打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集制度。這是關長的個案酌情權，不是持牌人自動享有的寬限期。', 'Where no eligible person has passed, the CCE may, as a matter of case-by-case discretion, allow the licensee to continue in business. If an exemption is granted, it carries licensing conditions that the CCE considers appropriate and necessary to ensure effective AML/CFT systems. This is the CCE’s individual discretion, not an automatic grace period for the licensee.'),
    ], [
        ref('01', '第4.4、8.1–8.3段', '¶4.4, 8.1–8.3', 'company-based qualification'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('參考：考試當日的操作細節（2022年須知）', 'Reference: practical arrangements on the day (2022 Notes)', [
        ('必須按照邀請信上的日期、時間和試場應考，不接受個別改期或更換試場的要求；開考後不准入場。未能出示所需文件，不准應考；受損或塗改的身分證件，可能不獲接納。不得未經許可離場；如果提早離場，須確保答卷及材料已被收回。任何已用或未用的問卷或答題紙，都不可帶走。對應：2022年考試須知。', 'Attend on the date and at the time and centre stated in the invitation. Individual requests to change the date or the centre are not considered, and entry is barred once the Assessment has started. Missing the required documents bars attendance. Damaged or defaced identification may be rejected. Do not leave without permission. Anyone who leaves early must ensure that the scripts and materials have been collected. No used or unused question book or answer sheet may be taken away. These arrangements are in the 2022 Notes.'),
        ('未獲准的物品須放在座位下，不能放在桌上、桌內、身上或衣袋裡。手機必須讓監考員看得見，並與其他電子或發聲裝置全程關機。不得不當通訊、滋擾、拍照、錄音或錄影，或抄走試題。這些是考場規則，並不是禁止把所有電子裝置帶進建築物。', 'Unauthorized articles must be placed under the chair, not on or in the desk, on the body or in a pocket. Phones must remain visible to the invigilators and must be switched off, together with other electronic or sound-emitting devices. Improper communication, disturbance, taking photographs, recording and copying questions are prohibited. These are examination-room rules, not a blanket ban on bringing every electronic device into the building.'),
        ('須按指示填上公司名稱、申請編號、姓名、公司職位、考試日期及簽署。正確塗黑答案、徹底擦除錯答、不要摺答題紙，並核對題號。答題時間過後，不接受更改。如有惡劣天氣的另行安排，會在其後首個工作日於 MSOS 網站公布。醫療及特殊協助安排，應按2022年須知及實際邀請或海關通知另行查閱。', 'Enter the company name, application number, candidate name, company position, assessment date and signature as instructed. Fill the answer boxes correctly, erase errors fully, do not fold the sheet, and check the question numbers. No changes are accepted after the allotted time. Any alternative severe-weather arrangements appear on MSOS on the following first working day. For health and special-assistance arrangements, consult the 2022 Notes and the actual invitation or Customs notices.'),
    ], [
        ref('01', '第9–11、13.1、14.2–14.3段', '¶9–11, 13.1, 14.2–14.3', 'the first working day that follows'),
    ], kind='reference'),
]),
section('licensing-actions', '表格、變更、續牌及結業實務', 'Forms, changes, renewal and cessation in practice', [
    block('事件與手續', 'Events and procedures', [
        ('續牌要用表格2，而且最遲須在屆滿前45日提交。海關一般會在屆滿前約90日發出提醒，但沒有收到提醒並不能免責。還須按通知期限交齊文件，並完成適用的評核；逾期或無效的申請，可以令牌照在屆滿時失效。例如：牌照在6月30日屆滿，表格2最遲須在5月16日或之前提交。即使沒有收到90日前的提醒，這個45日期限仍然適用。', 'A renewal is made on Form 2, and it has a hard filing deadline. Use Form 2 at least 45 days before expiry. Customs normally sends a reminder around 90 days before expiry, but the lack of a reminder is no excuse. Documents and any required assessment must also be completed by the notified deadlines. A late or invalid application can result in the licence lapsing. For example: if the licence expires on 30 June, Form 2 must be submitted no later than 16 May. The 45-day deadline still applies even if the 90-day reminder never arrived.'),
        ('新增董事、最終擁有人或合夥人，須用表格4事先申請；新增處所，或由沒有特定處所改為在特定處所經營，則用表格5。後者須按要求更新業務計劃及打擊洗錢政策。不能先開始營業或先讓人上任，再補交申請。', 'Use Form 4 for prior approval of a new director, ultimate owner or partner. Use Form 5 to add premises, or to move from no particular premises to particular premises. Where required, the business plan and the AML policy must also be updated. Do not start operating, or let the person take up the post, and only apply afterwards.'),
        ('一般資料變更用表格6，在改變當日起計一個月內通知，涵蓋名稱或聯絡、處所、銀行帳戶、業務、合規主任或洗錢報告主任等適用項目。如果兌換或匯款的業務性質有轉變，須書面通知並提交新的計劃或政策。法律實體本身改變，則必須重新申請牌照，不能只改資料。例如：把獨資改成有限公司，這是換了一個法律實體，須重新申牌，不是交一份表格6便可以。', 'Ordinary changes of particulars are notified on Form 6, within one month beginning on the date of the change. This covers applicable changes of name or contact details, premises, bank accounts, the business, and the CO or MLRO. A change between exchange and remittance activities requires written notification and an updated plan or policy. A change of legal entity requires a fresh licence application, not merely an update of particulars. For example: converting a sole proprietorship into a limited company is a change of legal entity. A new licence is required; Form 6 is not enough.'),
        ('結業或停止分行，須用表格7在停止之前通知，並在停止當日起計7日內交還牌照。如果停止全部特定處所，但仍想改為沒有特定處所的模式繼續經營，依指引必須重新申請，不能逕自把舊牌轉用。', 'For cessation, or the closure of a branch, use Form 7 to give notice before stopping, and return the licence within seven days beginning on the cessation date. If you close all particular premises but want to continue in the no-particular-premises mode, the Guide requires a fresh application. The old licence cannot simply be reused.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第6、8–10段', 'Sections 6, 8–10', 'Form 7'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('經營責任及銀行戶名', 'Operating duties and bank-account names', [
        ('持牌後仍須按牌照條件及法例營業。指引所列、並非盡列的經營責任，見下一段。用於金錢服務的銀行戶口，戶名必須符合指引：持牌公司，或持牌人的獨資經營者、合夥人、董事或最終擁有人；不是任何第三方的帳戶都可以使用。', 'After licensing, the business must still be operated under the licence and the law. The Guide’s non-exhaustive list of operating obligations is set out next. Bank accounts used for the money service must be in names permitted by the Guide: the licensed company, or the licensee’s proprietor, partner, director or ultimate owner. An account in an arbitrary third party’s name is not acceptable.'),
        ('持牌人的經營責任，指引另外列出一份並非詳盡無遺的清單。這些責任包括：(a) 報告可疑交易；(b) 制訂並維持有效的打擊洗錢政策；(c) 有關個人、任何合夥人、任何董事及最終擁有人在任何時間均是適當人選；(d) 取得混合式商住樓宇內處所每名佔用人的書面同意，讓獲授權人進行例行視察；(e) 在牌照指明的處所顯眼地方展示牌照正本；(f) 維持本地儲存帳目及紀錄地點；(g) 沒有特定處所經營時，維持本地管理辦事處，作為與海關溝通的聯絡點；(h) 確保最少一名高級管理層成員已應考能力評核；(i) 按時以指明格式遞交定期申報表；(j) 經營用的銀行帳戶屬於上述指定名下。對應：Licensing Guide paragraph 11.1。', 'The Guide also sets out a non-exhaustive list of a licensee’s operating obligations. Paragraph 11.1 lists licensee obligations (non-exhaustive): (a) report suspicious transactions; (b) develop and maintain an effective AML Policy; (c) the individual, any partner, any director and ultimate owner remain fit and proper at all times; (d) secure every occupant’s written consent for routine inspection by an authorized person at mixed commercial/residential premises; (e) display the original licence conspicuously at specified premises; (f) maintain an LPS; (g) without particular premises, maintain an LMO as the point of contact with C&ED; (h) ensure at least one senior manager has attended the Assessment; (i) submit periodic returns on time in the specified form; and (j) keep money-service bank accounts in the permitted names.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第11.1–11.3段', '¶11.1–11.3', 'Where bank account(s) is used'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('記憶：表格6所列的十四項變更', 'Remember: the fourteen Form 6 changes', [
        ('表格6涵蓋的變更，可以先記「業務及聯絡」這一組，一共七項：(a) 業務或法團名稱；(b) 主要（通訊）地址；(c) 聯絡資料；(d) 業務處所資料；(e) 業務處所電話或傳真；(f) 在處所經營的其他業務資料；(g) 商住處所佔用人。', 'The changes covered by Form 6 can first be remembered as the business and contact group, which has seven items: (a) business or corporation name; (b) principal or correspondence address; (c) contact information; (d) business-premises information; (e) premises telephone or fax; (f) other business operated at the premises; and (g) occupants of mixed commercial or residential premises.'),
        ('「人員及資格」是另外三項，而且不要把改資料、換人和資格改變當成同一件事。(h) 是獨資經營者、合夥人、董事或最終擁有人的詳情；(i) 是合夥人、董事或最終擁有人本身；(j) 是上述適用人士的適當人選身分。人的身分資料改變、換了人，以及適當人選資格改變，是三種不同項目。例如：董事只是改了電話號碼，屬詳情變更；換成另一名董事，是換人，通常還須事先批准；該人不再是適當人選，則是資格改變。', 'The people and fitness group has three further items, and a change of particulars, a change of person and a change of fitness status are not the same thing. They are: (h) particulars of the proprietor, partners, directors or ultimate owners; (i) the partners, directors or ultimate owners themselves; and (j) the relevant persons’ fit-and-proper status. A change in a person’s particulars, replacement of the person, and a change in fitness status, are three distinct items. For example: a director who only changes a telephone number is a change of particulars. Replacing that director with another person is a change of the person, and usually also needs prior approval. A finding that the person is no longer fit and proper is a change of fitness status.'),
        ('「經營安排」還有四項：(k) 金錢服務銀行帳戶；(l) 本地管理辦事處；(m) 本地紀錄儲存地方；(n) 合規主任或洗錢報告主任。新增董事、最終擁有人或合夥人，以及新增處所，另外還有事先批准的責任，見上文。適當人選身分變更，也可引致對牌照有效性的覆核。', 'The operating-arrangements group has four more items: (k) money-service bank accounts; (l) the LMO; (m) the LPS; and (n) the CO or MLRO. New directors, ultimate owners or partners, and additional premises, separately require prior approval, as described above. A change in fitness status can also trigger a review of whether the licence remains valid.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第8.1–8.4、9.1–9.3段', '¶8.1–8.4, 9.1–9.3', 'Change in occupants of the particular premises'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('續牌無效與持續經營的界線', 'Invalid renewal and the boundary of continuing operation', [
        ('續牌申請在三種情況之下會無效，而且任何一種已經足夠。不要把「已經開始填表」或「還在等文件」，當成已經有一份有效的續牌申請。這三種情況是：未在屆滿前45日交妥表格2、補充資料表格及相關附件；收到催交後，未在指明期限內交齊證明文件；或在須評核時，未在收到邀請後7日內提名合資格人士。對應：Licensing Guide paragraph 6.4。', 'A renewal application can be invalid in any one of three situations. Starting to fill in a form, or still waiting for documents, does not itself create a valid renewal application. Paragraph 6.4 gives three alternative invalidity grounds: failure to submit the completed Form 2, supplementary sheet and annex by 45 days before expiry; failure to provide all supporting documents within the specified period after a reminder; or, where assessment is required, no eligible nominee within seven days after receipt of the invitation.'),
        ('無效申請的後果，與第2部分所講「有效續牌申請尚待決定時牌照可繼續有效」，並不是同一回事。無效申請不能獲處理，原有牌照到期便自動失效，必須停止金錢服務。即使是因為牌照屆滿而停業，停業前仍須用表格7通知，並在自停業或屆滿日起計7日內交回有效或已屆滿的牌照。在有效期內取消牌照，不會獲退還全部或部分費用。', 'The consequence of an invalid application is not the same as the continuation that applies, as explained in Part 2, while a valid renewal is still awaiting determination. An invalid application cannot be processed; the old licence lapses at expiry and the money service must stop. Form 7 notice must still be given before cessation, including cessation on licence expiry, and the valid or expired licence must be returned within seven days beginning on cessation or expiry. Cancelling a licence during its validity brings no full or partial fee refund.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第6.3–6.4、10.2–10.3段', '¶6.3–6.4, 10.2–10.3', 'the existing licence will lapse automatically'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('維持牌照：九類撤銷／暫時吊銷例子', 'Maintaining a licence: nine examples of revocation/suspension grounds', [
        ('維持牌照之後，仍有一些情況可以成為撤銷或暫時吊銷的理由，而且清單並不是盡列的。這些例子包括：(a) 不再是適當人選；(b) 佔用人撤回進入同意；(c) 新佔用人拒絕同意；(d) 本地紀錄儲存地方欠缺或不合要求；(e) 在無特定處所模式下，本地管理辦事處欠缺或不合要求。', 'Once a licence has been granted, it can still be revoked or suspended in certain situations, and the list of examples is not exhaustive. The non-exhaustive paragraph 7.1 examples include (a) loss of fitness or propriety; (b) an occupant withdrawing entry consent; (c) a new occupant refusing consent; (d) an absent or non-compliant LPS; and (e) an absent or non-compliant LMO for no-particular-premises operation.'),
        ('同一段還有另外四類例子：(f) 定期申報逾期；(g) 持牌未達提供金錢服務的目的，例如從未提供服務；(h) 違反 AMLO 規定，包括第5部；(i) 未委任或維持合資格的合規主任或洗錢報告主任。關長可以撤銷或暫時吊銷，但須先給予陳詞機會及書面通知。這與 section 43 的譴責、補救命令及罰款，是不同的權力。', 'The same paragraph has four further examples. Also (f) late periodic returns; (g) failure to fulfil the licence’s purpose of providing a money service, such as never providing it; (h) AMLO breaches, including Part 5; and (i) failure to appoint or maintain a competent CO or MLRO. The CCE may revoke or suspend, after giving an opportunity to be heard and written notice. This is a different power from the reprimands, remediation orders and fines under section 43.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第7.1–7.3、13.1段', '¶7.1–7.3, 13.1', 'a money service has never been provided'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('penalty-factors', '罰款指引：上限不等於固定罰款', 'Penalty guidelines: a ceiling is not a fixed fine', [
    block('第12及13份指引的評估因素', 'Assessment under documents 12 and 13', [
        ('罰款指引裡的上限，不是每次違規都固定判那個數目。第12份屬發牌紀律罰款，section 43 最高港幣100萬元；第13份屬指明的盡職審查或紀錄等違規，section 21 最高為港幣1,000萬元，或利益或避免成本的3倍，以較大者為準。不是每次都固定判上限，也不是固定按利益的3倍來罰。', 'A ceiling in the penalty guidelines is not a fixed fine that is imposed in every case. Document 12 concerns section 43 licensing penalties, capped at HK$1 million. Document 13 concerns section 21 specified CDD or record-related contraventions, capped at the greater of HK$10 million or three times the profit gained or costs avoided. Neither the ceiling, nor a three-times figure, is an automatic penalty.'),
        ('評估罰款時，會考慮違規的性質、嚴重性、持續時間、是否故意或罔顧、是否系統性、造成的損害及所得利益；也會看糾正措施、合作或主動披露、過往紀錄、其他相關處分，以及處理上是否一致。罰款應有阻嚇力，並按整體情況考慮財政影響，不應有很可能令經營者陷入財務困境的效果。', 'When a pecuniary penalty is assessed, consider the nature, seriousness and duration of the contravention, whether it was intentional or reckless, whether it was systemic, the harm caused and the benefit obtained. Also consider remediation, cooperation or voluntary disclosure, history, other sanctions, and consistency of treatment. Penalties should deter. Financial impact is assessed in context, and should not have the likely effect of putting the operator into financial jeopardy.'),
    ], [
        ref('12', '第4–9段', '¶4–9', 'deterrent'),
        ref('13', '第3–9段', '¶3–9', 'three times'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('罰款評估的四組因素', 'Four groups used in pecuniary-penalty assessment', [
        ('第一組因素有九項，先記關於性質、嚴重性及影響的前四項：(i) 是蓄意、罔顧還是疏忽，純粹疏忽或技術性違規一般較輕；(ii) 持續時間及頻密程度；(iii) 是否可能損害香港作為國際金融中心的聲譽，第12份另外還提到金錢服務業務的廉潔穩健；(iv) 是否造成或可能造成他人損失，或使他人承擔支出，第12份亦明列可能使他人承擔支出。', 'The first group has nine nature, seriousness and impact factors. The first four are: (i) whether the conduct was intentional, reckless or negligent, with merely negligent or technical breaches generally being less serious; (ii) duration and frequency; (iii) potential harm to Hong Kong’s reputation as an international financial centre, with document 12 also naming the integrity of money-service operations; and (iv) actual or potential loss to others, or costs imposed on them, with document 12 expressly also covering potential costs.'),
        ('同一組接下來是：(v) 是獨自違規，還是作為某集團的一部分，以及在該集團中扮演的角色；(vi) 整體或部分業務的盡職審查及紀錄程序管理制度或內控，是否有嚴重或系統性弱點；(vii) 是否顯示一套導致違規的行事模式，或一套違規模式。單次孤立錯誤、共同參與及持續模式，不能一概只寫成「不合規」。', 'The next factors in the same group are: (v) whether the person acted alone or as part of a group, and the role played in that group; (vi) serious or systemic management or internal-control weaknesses in CDD and record procedures for all or part of the business; and (vii) a pattern of conduct resulting in contraventions, or a pattern of contraventions. An isolated error, participation in a group, and a continuing pattern, are not adequately described only as “non-compliance”.'),
        ('最後兩項是：(viii) 多項較小問題，單項未必足以施加罰款，但合併考慮後可以足以施罰；(ix) 該違規所促成、引致，或可歸因於該違規的任何金融罪行之性質及程度。如果只看有沒有實際金錢損失，便會漏掉系統風險、行為模式和金融罪行的影響。', 'The last two in this group are: (viii) smaller issues that may not individually justify a pecuniary penalty, but that do so when considered collectively; and (ix) the nature and extent of any financial crime facilitated, occasioned or otherwise attributable to the contravention. Looking only at actual monetary loss would miss systemic risk, patterns of conduct and the impact of financial crime.'),
        ('第二組看違規之後的行為，包括有沒有隱瞞、有沒有補救、是否合作，以及再犯風險。第三組看既往的紀律或合規紀錄，包括相類違規、過往承諾，以及其他機關已經採取或可能採取的處分。', 'The second group looks at conduct after the contravention: concealment, remediation, cooperation, and the risk of recurrence. The third group looks at disciplinary or compliance history: similar breaches, previous undertakings, and action that other authorities have taken or are likely to take.'),
        ('第四組是其他相關因素，包括行為當時有效的指引、與相類個案是否一致、得益或避免的成本，以及主動及完整披露等減輕因素。一般不會就符合當時有效指引的行為作出紀律處分；關長一般會公開罰款決定。這些是非盡列、按個案評估的指引，不是把每項因素固定加減分。', 'The fourth group covers other relevant factors: the guidance that was current at the time, consistency with similar cases, benefit or cost avoidance, and mitigating factors such as prompt and complete disclosure. Generally, no discipline is taken for conduct that was in line with the guidance then in force. Pecuniary decisions are usually publicized. These are non-exhaustive, case-specific factors, not a fixed points formula.'),
    ], [
        ref('12', '第4–9段', '¶4–9', 'generally the CCE will not take disciplinary action'),
        ref('13', '第3–9段', '¶3–9', 'Other relevant factors'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('exchange-note', '第34章：兌換交易單及顧客撤銷權', 'Cap.34: transaction notes and rescission', [
    block('適用範圍及交易步驟', 'Scope and transaction steps', [
        ('《貨幣兌換商條例》（第34章）並不是每一筆兌換都適用，而且它的金額界線與 AMLO 的盡職審查門檻並不相同。第34章不適用於認可機構、符合條件的酒店兌換，以及顧客交付款額超過港幣100,000元的交易。剛好港幣100,000元，仍在這個金額範圍之內。這與 AMLO 一般非經常交易盡職審查的港幣120,000元門檻，完全是兩套規則。這條所說的貨幣，也包括支票及旅行支票。例如：顧客拿出剛好港幣100,000元來兌換，第34章的交易單等規則仍然適用；不能因為記了 AMLO 的12萬元，就把這筆當成已經豁除第34章。', 'The Money Changers Ordinance, Cap. 34, does not apply to every exchange, and its monetary line is not the same as the AMLO CDD threshold. Cap. 34 excludes authorized institutions, qualifying hotel exchange, and transactions in which the customer tenders more than HK$100,000. Exactly HK$100,000 remains within that monetary scope. This is an entirely different rule from the AMLO general occasional-transaction CDD threshold of HK$120,000. “Currency” here also includes cheques and travellers’ cheques. For example: a customer who tenders exactly HK$100,000 for an exchange is still within Cap. 34, so the transaction-note rules still apply. The AMLO figure of HK$120,000 must not be used to treat this transaction as already excluded from Cap. 34.'),
        ('交易前須按附表1填具一式兩份交易單，內容包括日期、貨幣及金額、已包含所有收費的淨匯率、付予顧客的貨幣等值及總額（編號可以選填），以及中英文名稱、地址、電話等。收銀員須簽署，並在實際可行情況下解釋內容，以及要求顧客簽署。不同的售出貨幣須分開開單，並按交易單上的全額付款，不得另再扣費。', 'Before the exchange, prepare a transaction note in duplicate in accordance with Schedule 1. The note includes the date, the currencies and amounts, the net rate already inclusive of all charges, the equivalent amount of the currency issued and the total (serial or transaction numbers are optional), and bilingual name, address and telephone details. The cashier signs, explains the contents as far as practicable, and requests the customer’s signature. Use a separate note for each different currency sold, and pay the amount stated on the note without any further deduction.'),
        ('正本交給顧客，副本至少保存12個月，並供警務人員依法查閱。如果顧客在交易完成前拒絕，須立即退還全數款項。若違反第4條，顧客可在交易後3日內，依第5條撤銷該宗交易。例如：顧客當天兌換後回家才發現交易單上的匯率與告示不符，而且第4條確有被違反，他可以在交易日之後的3日內行使撤銷權。', 'Give the original to the customer. Keep the duplicate for at least 12 months, for lawful inspection by a police officer. If the customer refuses before the transaction is completed, the full amount must be returned immediately. Where section 4 is breached, the customer may rescind the transaction within three days under section 5. For example: a customer who later the same day finds that the rate on the note does not match the displayed rate, and section 4 has in fact been breached, may rescind within three days after the date of the transaction.'),
    ], [
        ref('17', '第2–5條及附表1', 'ss.2–5; Schedule 1', 'within 3 days after the date'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('正本、副本與簽署的要求', 'Original, duplicate and signature requirements', [
        ('兌換商須在正本及副本上簽署，並在切實可行範圍內解釋內容。還須請顧客簽署正本；若副本上尚未記錄該簽署的複本，亦須請顧客簽署副本。淨匯率必須已經包括收費或佣金，不可在交易單上另外再寫收費或佣金。只可加入法定准許的內容，不能任意附加免責條款。', 'The changer must sign both the original and the duplicate, and must explain the contents as far as practicable. Separately, the customer’s signature must be requested on the original, and also on the duplicate unless a copy of that signature is already recorded there. State the net rate inclusive of charges or commission, without a separate reference to those charges or commission on the note. Include only authorized content, not arbitrary disclaimers.'),
    ], [
        ref('17', '第4(1)–(4)條', 's.4(1)–(4)', 'unless a copy of the signature is recorded on the duplicate'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('exchange-display', '匯率展示、廣告及責任', 'Rate displays, advertising and liability', [
    block('買入／賣出從兌換商角度理解', 'Buying/selling from the changer’s perspective', [
        ('告示牌上展示的淨匯率，是已包括全部收費及佣金的每單位外幣港幣價格。對於附表3內，自己準備買入或賣出的貨幣，須在清楚、光線足夠而且沒有遮擋的告示牌上，展示相應的淨率；並不是強制買賣全部17種貨幣。如果有多塊牌子，匯率必須相同，並可按10或100單位列示。展示的是最不利率，但仍可以給顧客更佳的匯率。', 'The net rate displayed on a board is the Hong Kong-dollar price per unit of foreign currency, inclusive of all charges and commission. Display the applicable net rates for the Schedule 3 currencies that the changer is prepared to buy or sell, clearly, visibly and with adequate lighting. There is no requirement to trade all 17 currencies. If there is more than one board, the rates on them must be identical. Units of 10 or 100 may be used. Display the least favourable rate; a better rate may still be offered to the customer.'),
        ('附表3列出17種貨幣：澳洲、加拿大、中國（不包括香港、澳門、台灣）、歐盟、印度、印尼、日本、馬來西亞、菲律賓、韓國、新加坡、瑞士、台灣、泰國、英國、美國及越南。第16份通函解釋了自2025年8月24日起生效的附表更新。', 'Schedule 3 lists 17 currencies: Australia, Canada, China excluding Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, the EU, India, Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia, the Philippines, Korea, Singapore, Switzerland, Taiwan, Thailand, the United Kingdom, the United States and Vietnam. Document 16 explains the amendments that took effect on 24 August 2025.'),
        ('未列於附表3的貨幣，在收取款項之前，須以書面向顧客提供買入及賣出兩個淨率，並另外遵守交易單規則。不能只因為某種貨幣不在展示清單上，便省略報價或交易單。', 'For a currency that is not on Schedule 3, both the buy and the sell net rates must be given to the customer in writing before money is accepted, and the transaction-note rules must also be followed. The fact that a currency is absent from the display list does not dispense with quotation or with the note.'),
        ('廣告裡的買入率與賣出率必須同等顯著。不得宣傳收取或不收取佣金或其他收費，也不得就匯率、條款或條例是否適用作出誤導。附表2允許的告示，包括顧客須自行承擔外幣管制限制，以及在離開前核對款項；這不是可以任意添加免責條款的許可。', 'In an advertisement, the buy and sell rates must be given equal prominence. Do not advertise that commission or other fees are, or are not, charged, and do not mislead about rates, terms or whether the Ordinance applies. Schedule 2 permits notices about the customer’s responsibility for currency-control restrictions, and about checking the money before leaving. That is not a licence to add arbitrary disclaimers.'),
        ('僱員違例，可以令僱主，以及符合條件的公司高級人員或合夥人一同負責，但法定的合理防止措施等抗辯另當別論。第4條初次違規屬第1級罰款（港幣2,000元），再次違規屬第2級罰款（港幣5,000元）及監禁6個月；第6、7、8、10條違規可處第2級罰款（港幣5,000元）及監禁6個月。', 'A breach by an employee can also engage the employer, and a qualifying corporate officer or partner, subject to statutory defences such as the taking of reasonable preventive steps. A first offence against section 4 carries a level 1 fine (HK$2,000). A subsequent offence carries a level 2 fine (HK$5,000) and six months. Offences against sections 6, 7, 8 and 10 carry a level 2 fine (HK$5,000) and six months.'),
    ], [
        ref('16', '正文第1頁', 'Main text p.1', '24 August 2025'),
        ref('17', '第6–11條及附表2–3', 'ss.6–11; Schedules 2–3', 'least favourable'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('同板比較及法定責任推定', 'Same-board comparison and statutory liability presumptions', [
        ('同一種貨幣的買入匯率和賣出匯率，必須同等顯眼，並且要讓顧客不必參看多於一塊告示牌，便能比較兩者。多塊牌子的匯率必須一致，與「可以在同一塊牌上比較買賣率」，是兩項相關但不同的條件。例如：把買入率寫在門口一塊牌，把賣出率寫在櫃檯另一塊牌，即使兩塊牌的數字各自正確，顧客仍須參看多於一塊牌才能比較，這並不符合這項要求。', 'The buying and selling rates for the same currency must be equally prominent, and a customer must be able to compare them without referring to more than one board. The requirement that rates on several boards be identical, and the requirement that both rates can be compared on one board, are related but distinct conditions. For example: putting the buy rate on a board at the door and the sell rate on a different board at the counter, even if each figure is accurate, still requires the customer to look at more than one board in order to compare them, and does not meet this requirement.'),
        ('在指定情況下，僱員的違規可以連繫到僱主，並可涉及公司董事、經理、秘書、相類高級人員及合夥人。沒有相反證據時，適用的人會被推定未採取合理的防止措施；必須連同法定適用身分及合理防止抗辯一起理解。僅僅提供專業意見，並不會單因此使人成為董事慣常依其指示行事的人。對應：Cap. 34 section 11。', 'In the specified situations, an employee’s breach can be linked to the employer, and can also engage directors, managers, secretaries, similar officers and partners, within the section’s scope. In the absence of contrary evidence, the applicable persons face a presumption that they failed to take reasonable preventive steps, subject to the statutory description of who is caught and to the defence. Giving professional advice alone does not make the adviser the person whose directions the directors habitually follow. This is Cap. 34 section 11.'),
    ], [
        ref('17', '第8(1)(b)、11條', 'ss.8(1)(b), 11', 'without the need to refer to more than one board'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
])
